The couples dance each week in a live show. The judges score each performance out of ten. After all the couples have danced they are then ranked according to the judges' scores and given points according to their rank, with the highest ranked couple receiving a number of points equal to the number of couples dancing that week e.g. 7 points where there are 7 couples dancing. When there are no tied scores the lowest scored couple will receive one point. However, in the event of a tie where two or more couples obtain the same judges score, the couple below those in the tie will be awarded one point below the points awarded to each of the tied couples. So, for example, if two couples obtain the same rank and obtain 7 points each, the couple immediately below them will be awarded 6 points. When couples are ranked equally by the judges the scoring of all other couples underneath will follow in the same descending order. Should there be any tied scores the lowest scored couple will therefore receive more than one point from the judges scores. The public are also invited to vote for their favourite couples, and the couples are ranked again according to the number of votes they receive, again receiving points; The couple with the most votes receiving the most points. Again in the unlikely event of a tie in the public vote the points are awarded in the same way as the points from the judges score.<ref name="format">{{cite web |title=BBC One – Strictly Come Dancing – About |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/16rGc8M34fT0wWYmrSMc8Cp/about |access-date=2025-10-01 |website=BBC |language=en-GB}}</ref>

The points for judges' score and public vote are then added together, and the two couples with the fewest points are placed in the bottom two. If two couples have equal points, the points from the public vote are given precedence. As with the previous series, the bottom two couples have to perform a dance-off on the results show. Based on that performance alone, each judge then votes on which couple should stay and which couple should leave.<ref name="format" /> For the first time in the show's history, the casting vote was not made solely by the head judge in the dance-off and was instead rotated, with a different judge making the decision each week.<ref>{{cite web |last=White |first=Adam |title=Strictly Come Dancing announces shocking vote twist that ‘will change everything’ |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/strictly-shirley-deciding-vote-dance-off-change-b2835068.html |language=en-gb |work=[[The Independent]] |date=27 September 2025 |access-date=5 October 2025}}</ref>

== Professional dancers ==
In April 2025, the BBC announced that all the professional dancers from the previous series; [[Dianne Buswell]], [[Nadiya Bychkova]], [[Amy Dowden]], [[Karen Hauer]], [[Katya Jones]], [[Neil Jones (dancer)|Neil Jones]], [[Nikita Kuzmin]], [[Gorka Márquez]], [[Luba Mushtuk]], [[Jowita Przystał]], [[Johannes Radebe]], [[Aljaž Škorjanec]], [[Kai Widdrington]], [[Nancy Xu]], [[Carlos Gu]], [[Lauren Oakley]], [[Michelle Tsiakkas]] and [[Vito Coppola]]; would be returning to this series.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=Professional Dancers confirmed as ''Strictly Come Dancing'' returns to BBC One and BBC iPlayer in autumn 2025 |date=11 April 2025 |publisher=[[BBC]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-professional-dancers-confirmed |access-date=11 April 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250731205213/https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-professional-dancers-confirmed |archive-date=31 July 2025}}</ref> On 27 July, the BBC announced that two new professional dancers, [[Alexis Warr]] and [[Julian Caillon]], would join the series.<ref name="NewPros">{{Cite press release |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' announces two new Professional Dancers |date=27 July 2025 |publisher=[[BBC]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-two-new-pros |access-date=27 July 2025 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20250727144558/https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-two-new-pros |archive-date=27 July 2025}}</ref> Warr won the [[So You Think You Can Dance (American TV series) season 17|seventeenth season]] of ''[[So You Think You Can Dance (American TV series)|So You Think You Can Dance]]'' and was a [[Dance troupe|troupe]] member on the American version of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]''.<ref name="NewPros" /> Caillon appeared as a professional dancer on three series of the Australian version of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (Australian TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]''.<ref name="NewPros" />

During the launch show, Julian Caillon and Alexis Warr received a celebrity partner for the first time, while Neil Jones, Gorka Márquez, Luba Mushtuk, Michelle Tsiakkas and Nancy Xu did not receive a partner. The rest of the pros were paired to a celebrity.<ref name="couples">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-2025-couples-revealed-launch-show |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' 2025 couples revealed in launch show |publisher=[[BBC]] |date=2025-09-20 |access-date=2025-09-20 |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-2025-couples-confirmed-newsupdate |title=''Strictly Come Dancing'' confirms couples for star-studded 2025 season |website=[[Radio Times]] |first=Katelyn |last=Mensah |date=2025-09-20 |access-date=2025-09-20 |language=en-GB}}</ref>

==Couples==
On 11 August 2025, [[Harry Aikines-Aryeetey]] was announced as the first contestant to be competing in the series on ''[[Newsround]]''.<ref>{{cite web |title=Olympian and Gladiator Harry Aikines-Aryeetey aka Nitro is the first celebrity contestant confirmed for Strictly Come Dancing 2025 |url=https://bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-harry-aikines-aryeetey-aka-nitro |website=[[BBC Media Centre]] |date=11 August 2025 |access-date=11 August 2025 |language=en-gb}}</ref> [[Dani Dyer]], [[Alex Kingston]] and [[Jimmy Floyd Hasselbaink]] were subsequently confirmed later that evening on ''[[The One Show]]''.<ref>{{cite web |title=Strictly Come Dancing announces Dani Dyer, Alex Kingston and Jimmy Floyd Hasselbaink for 2025 lineup |url=https://independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/strictly-come-dancing-cast-lineup-dani-dyer-b2805684.html |website=[[The Independent]] |first1=Ellie |last1=Muir |first2=Jacob |last2=Stolworthy |access-date=12 August 2025 |date=11 August 2025 |language=en-gb}}</ref> The celebrities continued to be revealed until 15 August 2025, when the full line-up was announced.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://manchestereveningnews.co.uk/news/tv/bbc-strictly-come-dancing-2025-32280817 |title=BBC Strictly Come Dancing 2025 line-up in full as 15 celebrities confirmed |website=[[Manchester Evening News]] |first1=Elizabeth |last1=Cotton |author2=Celebrity Writer |access-date=15 August 2025 |date=15 August 2025 |language=en-gb}}</ref> ''[[Game of Thrones]]'' actor and DJ [[Kristian Nairn]] was initially announced as the final celebrity to be competing in the series, however on 21 August 2025, he withdrew from the competition due to health reasons.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Rawlinson |first1=Kevin |title=Game of Thrones actor Kristian Nairn pulls out of Strictly Come Dancing |url=https://theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/aug/21/game-of-thrones-actor-kristian-nairn-pulls-out-strictly-come-dancing |website=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=21 August 2025 |date=21 August 2025}}</ref> Former ''[[Emmerdale]]'' actor [[Lewis Cope]] was subsequently announced as his replacement on ''The One Show'' later that evening.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c74d71j4433o |title=Game of Thrones star withdraws from Strictly with stress |website=[[BBC]] |first1=Ian |last1=Youngs |access-date=21 August 2025 |date=21 August 2025 |language=en-gb}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Actor Lewis Cope joins the cast of Strictly Come Dancing 2025 |url=https://bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2025/strictly-come-dancing-lewis-cope/ |access-date=2025-08-21 |website=[[BBC]] |language=en}}</ref> On 23 September 2025, ''[[Love Island (2015 TV series)|Love Island]]'' winner and actress Dani Dyer, who was initially announced as a contestant and was paired up with [[Nikita Kuzmin]] during the launch show, was announced to be withdrawing from the series after fracturing her ankle during training,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c98d6z1j9neo |title=Dani Dyer pulls out of Strictly with broken ankle |website=[[BBC]] |first=Ian |last=Youngs |date=23 September 2025 |accessdate=23 September 2025 |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a68020095/strictly-dani-dyer-quit-2025-injury/ |title=Strictly's Dani Dyer quits 2025 series after launch show |website=[[Digital Spy]] |first=Emily |last=Stedman  |date=23 September 2025 |accessdate=23 September 2025 |language=en-GB}}</ref> ''[[Love Island (2015 TV series)|Love Island]]'' winner and [[West End theatre|West End]] actress [[Amber Davies]] was announced as her replacement on 26 September, and began training with Kuzmin ahead of the first live show the following evening.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cp8w0zx58neo |title=Actress and West End star Amber Davies joins Strictly line-up |website=[[BBC]] |first=Helen |last=Bushby |date=26 September 2025 |accessdate=26 September 2025 |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/strictly-come-dancing-amber-davies-joins-line-up-newsupdate |title=Strictly Come Dancing confirms Dani Dyer replacement - and it's another Love Island winner |website=[[Radio Times]] |first=Katelyn |last=Mensah |date=26 September 2025 |accessdate=26 September 2025 |language=en-GB}}</ref>

